  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "... at least, they don't work for the config/rest/*.xslt files.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I think the root of the problem is in the GTransformer class.  It looks to me like most calls to getTransformer end up passing in a null URI resolver rather than a resolver that knows how to resolve relative URIs.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Whatever the reason, having to specify absolute pathnames   in xsl:include directives is messy and introduces unwanted deployment problems.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
